comments.body:
I spent a bit of time tracing through the code in the debugger.  @participant2 I tried what you said but it didn't seem to help.  May not have done it in the right place though.  I tried to replaced the `FORMAT_NONE` with `FORMAT_PANE|wp->id` in the `format_create` call in `window_tree_get_key` and when that didn't help, I noticed that there were several other calls to `format_single`, which calls `format_create_defaults` which in turn calls `format_create`, so I changed it in there too after checking if wp!=NULL.  Nope, that didn't help either.  I am not sure what the `FORMAT_FORCE` flag does but I also tried adding that too.

Clearly I need to better understand the code more to figure out what's going on.  

@reporter it sounds like what you want is a new format variable containg the session's `status-right` which might imply other variables as well.  Or perhaps a new format variable for just the pane's cpu_time, that's up to @participant2.  What I think you were trying to do when you ran across this was to use `#()` to execute some sort of shell cmd like `ps | grep #{pane_pid} | sed ...` or something to pick out the cpu time for the pid.
